dataset(wages).add(none = 0 * union).glm(none ~ educ, family: binomial)
---
error[Z0803]: glm: `none` is 0 in every row used, so maximum likelihood does not exist
 --> scripts/main.zeff:1:38
  |
1 | dataset(wages).add(none = 0 * union).glm(none ~ educ, family: binomial)
  |                                      ^^^ an outcome that does not vary
  |
  = help: the probability of a 1 would be 0 whatever the regressors; check how `none` was coded and which rows were dropped for NA

